---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Hands-on design leader specializing in human-centered transformation" showBackButton={true}>
  <section class="case-study-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        Hands-on design leader with 15+ years of experience building human-centered
        organizations that create human-centered products.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-study-content">
    <div class="container content">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I design and I build. Specs, prototypes written in real code against real
        APIs, and the version that ships. At Bibel TV around 70% of what I
        prototype reaches production with minor modification, and iteration
        moved from days to hours. Engineering there is an external agency, so
        that handoff crosses a company boundary and holds anyway.
      </p>

      <h2>Leading</h2>
      <p>
        When a collaboration keeps failing, the instinct is to manage the
        person. I have had better results changing the conditions: written
        agendas, material sent ahead, decisions recorded, turn-taking on
        purpose. That turned a working relationship the team had learned to
        route around into one of its strongest contributors.
      </p>
      <p>
        You cannot build inclusive software with an exclusive team process.
      </p>

      <h2>Regulated environments</h2>
      <p>
        Most of my career has been inside software that cannot be casually
        instrumented. Five years at Datameer, building analytics used by
        analysts inside top US, Canadian and UK banks and insurers. Then
        ChurchDesk, a platform for churches across six countries under GDPR plus
        Protestant and Catholic data-protection law, where I shipped AI alt-text
        for EU accessibility compliance.
      </p>

      <h2>Now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bibel TV</strong> — Head of Product Design. A design system synced across platforms, an AI support copilot in daily production use, and the app redesign.</li>
        <li><strong>"Designing with and for AI"</strong> — a workshop series I have run since 2024 with a partner agency, teaching teams to work with AI tools rather than around them.</li>
        <li><strong>M.A. Leadership</strong> — Kairos University, completed 2026.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Let's Talk</h2>
      <p>
        I'm based in Berlin, Germany.
      </p>

      </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
